T2b   | RECORD      |     3.877e+00 | erank(Rt) < 0.9*Nt ?    | erank(Rt) = 3.8770/4 (0.969), erank(Rr) = 7.3500/8 (0.919), erank(C_ens) = 28.4958/32 (0.890); DECISION: pilots = DFT (transmit side near-white, eigen-alignment is meaningless); Rt eigenvalues = [1.2103, 1.0857, 0.9776, 0.7264]. THE DECISION IS TAKEN ON Rt, because the pilots span the TRANSMIT side (Y = H Xp); erank(C_ens) is reported but does NOT decide. The full-covariance reading (erank(C_ens) = 28.4958 < 0.9*32 = 28.8000) would have said eigen-aligned (informative) -- IT DIFFERS from the decision in force. Knife edge: Rt is 0.969 of full and C_ens is 0.890, on opposite sides of 0.9. The choice is recorded here so it is auditable, not invisible.
